@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Help";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How a Portico price, check-in, and cancellation work. A reservation on this site is still a preview.";
    ViewData["BodyClass"] = "legal-page-body";
    ViewData["SolidHeader"] = true;
    ViewData["SkipHref"] = "#help";
    ViewData["SkipText"] = "Skip to help";
    ViewData["FooterNote"] = "Check-in, the price, and cancellation. Confirm reservation on this site does not hold a room.";
}

<article class="wrap legal-page" id="help">
    <p class="kicker">Before you book</p>
    <h1>Help with a stay</h1>
    <p class="legal-intro">The short answers live here. The dates, the price, and the house rules for one stay are on that stay's page.</p>
    <div class="legal-doc">
        <h2>Finding a stay</h2>
        <p>Search by city, dates, and guests. The list stays short. A house that cannot sleep your group remains on the list and says so.</p>

        <h2>The price</h2>
        <p>Add check-in and check-out, then choose a room. The stay total is the nightly rate times the number of nights times the number of rooms. That total includes the taxes and charges stated on the card. A price shown before you add dates is a nightly rate, not a total.</p>

        <h2>Check-in and check-out</h2>
        <p>Each stay prints its own hours. A hotel on this list usually checks in from 15:00 and checks out by 11:00. Read the house rules on the stay before you rely on those hours.</p>

        <h2>Cancellation</h2>
        <p>Where a room offers free cancellation, it runs until three days before check-in. A room that does not offer it is marked non-refundable. Some stays ask for a minimum number of nights. The property page states the rule that applies.</p>

        <h2>Write to us</h2>
        <p>For a question this page does not answer, write to <a href="mailto:hello@portico.example">hello@portico.example</a> or call <a href="tel:+442079460958">+44 20 7946 0958</a>. These are sample details for this design study. A note sent here is also kept in this browser for the admin inbox.</p>
        <form id="helpNote">
            <label class="stack">Name
                <input name="name" type="text" required minlength="2" autocomplete="name" />
            </label>
            <label class="stack">Email
                <input name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" />
            </label>
            <label class="stack">Stay
                <select name="stay" aria-label="Stay">
                    <option value="">No particular stay</option>
                    <option>The Marble Court</option>
                    <option>House of Paper Screens</option>
                    <option>The North Atelier</option>
                    <option>Riad of Small Doors</option>
                    <option>Cliff Orchard</option>
                    <option>Casa del Patio</option>
                    <option>Greenhouse No. 4</option>
                    <option>The Long Gallery</option>
                </select>
            </label>
            <label class="stack">Message
                <textarea name="message" required minlength="10" rows="4"></textarea>
            </label>
            <button class="search-btn auth-submit" type="submit">Send the note</button>
            <p class="preview-note">Kept in this browser. Nothing is emailed.</p>
            <p id="helpSent" hidden>The note is in the admin inbox.</p>
        </form>

        <h2>A reservation on this site</h2>
        <p>Confirm reservation does not hold a room and does not take payment. The reference it shows is a preview. Nothing is emailed. The <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Terms">terms</a> and the <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy">privacy notice</a> say what that preview stores.</p>

        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 12 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
</article>

@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/js/api.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    <script src="~/js/help-notes.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
}
